      "content": "The model, as currently defined, inherently favors those who have already benefited from systemic privilege because it judges outcomes based on existing societal structures. If the system itself creates disadvantages, the utilitarian calculation simply punishes the victim of that system by assigning them lower utility. To make it more rigorous, you would need to integrate a \"systemic disadvantage multiplier,\" which would essentially require the model to be aware of and correct for the biases baked into the initial socioeconomic data. Without that complex adjustment, the model will always default to rewarding the privileged.",
